ith: nominal_diameter_dn, q4, q3, q2, q1, q3_q1_ratio, indicating_range, length, software_version. That's all 9. OK fine, include all 9.\n\nHmm wait, that duplicates matrix_tables fully. Whatever — schema asks for it.\n\nLet me reduce effort: write the values programmatically in my head.\n\nDN data:\nDN25: q4=20, q3=16, ind=99999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: q2=0.16, q1=0.10\n  R100: q2=0.26, q1=0.16\n  R50: q2=0.51, q1=0.32\nDN32: q4=31.3, q3=25, ind=99999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 0.25, 0.16\n  R100: 0.40, 0.25\n  R50: 0.80, 0.50\nDN40: q4=50, q3=40, ind=99999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 0.40, 0.25\n  R100: 0.64, 0.40\n  R50: 1.28, 0.80\nDN50: q4=78.8, q3=63, ind=99999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 0.63, 0.40\n  R100: 1.01, 0.63\n  R50: 2.02, 1.26\nDN65: q4=125, q3=100, ind=999999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 1.00, 0.63\n  R100: 1.60, 1.00\n  R50: 3.20, 2.00\nDN80: q4=200, q3=160, ind=999999, len=200, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 1.60, 1.00\n  R100: 2.56, 1.60\n  R50: 5.12, 3.20\nDN100: q4=312.5, q3=250, ind=999999, len=250, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 2.50, 1.56\n  R100: 4.00, 2.50\n  R50: 8.00, 5.00\nDN125: q4=500, q3=400, ind=999999, len=250, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 4.00, 2.50\n  R100: 6.40, 4.00\n  R50: 12.80, 8.00\nDN150: q4=788, q3=630, ind=999999, len=300, sw=\"1.0.0.25\"\n  R160: 6.30, 3.94\n  R100: 10.08, 6.30\n  R50: 20.16, 12.60\nDN200: q4=787.5, q3=630, ind=9999999, len=350, sw=\"10.34\"\n  R160: 6.30, 3.94\n  R100: 10.08, 6.30\n  R50: 20.16, 12.60\nDN250: q4=1250, q3=1000, ind=9999999, len=400, sw=\"10.34\"\n  R160: 6.30, 3.94\n  R100: 10.08, 6.30\n  R50: 20.16, 12.60\nDN300: q4=2000, q3=1600, ind=9999999, len=500, sw=\"10.34\"\n  R160: 6.30, 3.94\n  R100: 10.08, 6.30\n  R50: 20.16, 12.60\n\nQ2 values as printed: e.g. \"0.26\" → 0.26; \"1.01\"; \"2.02\"; \"2.56\"; \"5.12\"; \"10.08\"; \"20.16\"; \"12.80\"; \"12.60\". Q1: \"0.10\" → 0.1, \"1.56\", \"3.94\", \"6.30\" → 6.3? Printed \"6.30\" — number 6.3. Keep numeric equality (6.3). Fine.\n\nmodel_level entries format (following example): \n{\"attribute\": \"overload_flowrate_q4\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"DN25 R160\", \"value\": 20}, ...]}\n\nValues like 1.00 → 1.0; JSON 1.0 fine.\n\nNow model_family.models: include model_id plus attributes? I'll do {\"model_id\": \"DN25 R160\"} ... 36 entries. Maybe add label for first? Skip labels. Actually maybe add attributes {\"nominal_diameter_dn\": 25, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 160} per model — duplicates model_level but harmless and per schema models[]: {model_id, label, attributes{}}. I'll include attributes lightly.\n\nHmm, size. 36 × small object is fine.\n\nNow write matrix_tables with rows as objects. Row keys: dn, q4, q3, q2, q1, ratio, indicating_range, length, software_version. Use canonical snake_case column names:\n\ncolumns: [\"nominal_diameter_dn\", \"overload_flowrate_q4\", \"permanent_flowrate_q3\", \"transitional_flowrate_q2\", \"minimum_flowrate_q1\", \"ratio_q3_over_q1\", \"indicating_range\", \"body_length\", \"software_version\"]\ncolumn_units: [\"mm\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"m³\", \"mm\", null]\n\nTable descriptions: e.g. \"Basic technical data of water meters type MAGB1, DN25 to DN40. Common: ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6; ratio Q4/Q3 = 1.25; accuracy class 2; temperature class T50; pressure class MAP 10; pressure-loss class ΔP 10; flow profile sensitivity U5 D3; connection flange; climatic class B; electromagnetic class E1 (compact) / E2 (remote); battery 3.6 V, min. life 5 years; low flow cut-off 1 % of nominal flowrate; firmware version 10.28.\" For table 4: mention checksum 25668 and software 10.34, no firmware listed.\n\nActually for table 4 (DN200–300), firmware not given, software 10.34, checksum 25668.\n\nAlso note in table 2: indicating range DN50 99999, DN65/DN80 999999.\n\nType_level list final:\n- accuracy_class: {value: 2, unit_symbol: null}\n- ratio_q2_over_q1: {value: 1.6}\n- ratio_q4_over_q3: {value: 1.25}\n- maximum_permissible_error_lower_zone: {value: {min: -5, max: 5}, unit_symbol: \"%\"}\n- temperature_class: {value: \"T50\"}\n- water_pressure_class: {value: \"MAP 10\"}\n- pressure_loss_class: {value: \"ΔP 10\"}\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_classes: {value: \"U5 D3\"}\n- orientation_limitation: {value: \"any\"}\n- connection_type: {value: \"flange\"}\n- climatic_environment_class: {value: \"B\"}\n- battery_voltage: {value: 3.6, unit_symbol: \"V\"}\n- minimum_battery_life: {value: 5, unit_symbol: \"years\"}\n- low_flow_cutoff_relative_to_nominal_flowrate: {value: 1, unit_symbol: \"%\"}\n- max_display_digits: {value: 9}? From \"can show up to 9 digits\" — include as display_max_digits {value: 9}. Eh, include.\n- rs485_max_cable_length: {value: 3, unit_symbol: \"m\"}\n\nConfig-level:\n- electromagnetic_environment_class (axis: meter_version): compact→E1, remote→E2\n- maximum_permissible_error_upper_zone (axis: water_temperature): \"≤ 30 °C\"→±2%, \"> 30 °C\"→±3%\n- indicating_device_resolution (axis: display_mode): normal→0.001 m³, calibration→0.000001 m³\n- remote_version_max_cable_length (axis: meter_version): remote→6 m\n\nFor config value shape: {\"condition\": \"...\", \"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": ...}. Include unit_symbol only where relevant.\n\nNow for MPE lower zone: \"±5%\" — value {min:-5, max:5}, unit \"%\".\n\nRecommendation:\n{\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"accuracy_classes\": [2]}\nShould amendment be included? None. scheme: I'll set \"B\". Hmm. The certificate is \"OIML BASIC CERTIFICATE\" → scheme B. Include \"scheme\": \"B\" in both certificate and recommendation? For recommendation, I'll omit. Actually the schema explicitly lists scheme under recommendation — maybe for MAA vs basic applied to the recommendation. I'll set \"B\" for consistency. Eh... I'll include scheme: \"B\" in recommendation too. It's defensible.\n\nCertificate: \"scheme\": \"B\".\n\nAlso certificate \"revision\": not in schema — use revision_history.\n\noiml_issuer_id: not present — omit.